# Dias Reference Map

External Dias artifacts (artworks, Arweave, social posts, NFC, physical objects, Easter eggs) use permanent IDs of the form `DIAS-{UUIDv4}`.

- Spec: `agent/DIAS-REFERENCE-MAP.md`
- Map data: `agent/dias-map.yaml`
- Agent index: `AGENTS.md`

## Core rule

`DIAS GUID -> canonical Markdown file`

`file` paths in the map are relative to the **repo root**, not to `agent/`.

Optional fields only: `note`, `link`. Omit `link` when discovery should stay hard. Do not turn the map into a second lore database.

## When capturing a reference

1. Preserve a user-supplied ID exactly, or generate a new UUID v4 prefixed with `DIAS-`.
2. Never reuse or replace an existing ID.
3. Point `file` at the best existing Markdown entry; do not create a lore file just for a GUID.
4. Add the entry to `agent/dias-map.yaml`.

## Protected files

Before deleting, moving, renaming, merging, or replacing Markdown, read `agent/dias-map.yaml`. Any file listed there is externally referenced. Update the map in the same change if a path moves. Prefer marking superseded canon over deleting it.

## Never

- delete or reuse a Dias GUID
- change a GUID's meaning
- leave dangling `file` paths after restructuring
